  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Compute class is a bound",
      "items": [
        "The selector chooses a configured target, login and optional compute type.",
        "Overflow stays within that type and never escalates to another login or target."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Occupied capacity",
      "items": [
        "One shared budget covers adapters, catalog loading and cleanup.",
        "Idle pooled physical connections can still occupy capacity and may be reclaimed. Active work is not reclaimed.",
        "Acquisition waits and retries within its deadline; the failure branch represents a timeout or cancellation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Transaction example",
      "items": [
        "BEGIN; first data query retains route reporting / finance_reader.",
        "Later data queries still select a route. A conflicting route is rejected. Cache is bypassed.",
        "After a query failure, roll back before more queries. COMMIT or ROLLBACK ends the retained block."
      ]
    }
